{
  "id": "payment_systems",
  "title": "Online merchant payment gateway",
  "case_type": "payment systems",
  "scenario": "Head of Payments: We are building a payment gateway that lets online merchants accept card and UPI payments through a hosted checkout page and an API. Payments must be authorised in real time, and the gateway must handle our festival-season peaks without problems. Security lead: We never want raw card numbers in our own database; cards must be tokenised through a certified vault. All payment traffic must use TLS, and card verification codes must never be stored. Repeated failed payment attempts from the same card or device should be blocked. Merchant success manager: Merchants want our gateway to save each customer's full card details for one-click repeat purchases, and they need daily settlement reports and the ability to issue refunds from a merchant dashboard. Compliance officer: Every transaction must be logged so that it can be audited, and suspicious patterns such as many small payments just under a reporting limit must be flagged for review. Merchant onboarding needs KYC of the business and of its directors. Operations: The gateway must be highly available. Settlements are paid into merchant bank accounts every day at 6 pm. Engineering manager: We deploy several times a day, and every change has to pass automated security scanning in the delivery pipeline before it reaches production. Finance: Our fee is a percentage of each transaction, with lower rates for high-volume merchants, and every customer must receive a payment receipt.",
